Console IO Instructions:

Valid Commands:
- help: Displays a help message with reminders of valid commands and their parameters.

- quit: Exits the program.

- add <referenceNumber>: adds a course instance from the database to the current schedule.
    <referenceNumber> must be a valid int id of an existing course instance in the database.

- remove <referenceNumber>: removes a course instance from the current schedule.
    <referenceNumber> must be a valid int id of an existing course instance in the database.

- save: Saves the current schedule to the database.
    NOTE: this has not been finished, and is waiting on Jon's db shortcuts class

- load <schedule>: Loads a schedule from the database into currentSchedule.
    <schedule> must be a valid int id of an existing schedule of the current student

- delete <schedule>: Deletes a schedule from the database.
    <schedule> must be a valid int id of an existing schedule of the current student

- new: Creates a new schedule for the current student.  This schedule becomes the current schedule.

- filter <filter type> <filter value>: Filters the current schedule by the given filter type and value.
    <filter type> must be one of the following:
        days
        start
        end
        session
        courseCode
        department
    <filter value> must be a valid value for the given filter type.
        for filter type days, filter value must be one of the following:
            MWF
            TR
        for filter type start and end, filter value must be a valid time in the format HH:MM:SS, eg 13:00:00 for 1pm or 08:00:00 for 8am
        for filter type session, filter value must be one of the following:
            FALL
            WINTER
            SPRING
            EARLYSUMMER
            LATESUMMER
        for filter type courseCode, filter value must be a list of course codes, the numbers only, separated by commas and spaces, eg 161, 478, 230
        for filter type department, filter value must be a 4-letter department code, eg COMP, MATH, CHEM

- search <keywords>: Searches the database for course instances that match the given keywords.
    <keywords> must be a list of keywords, eg math 161 comp 350

- print <referenceNumber>: Prints the details of a course instance with the given reference number.
    <referenceNumber> must be a valid int id of an existing course instance in the database.

- schedule: Prints the details of all course instances in current schedule to the console.